      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMHO, trusty_reclaim_memory() will fail only in a linux-compromised scenario. In that case, bad args may have prevented trusty from releasing resource on the trusty-side. Also, in this scenario, we can not ensure trusty releases access and if that impacts linux, which is already compromised, the impact can not be avoided. That is why I was originally returning an error-code so that the system can/should reboot in this situation.",
