      "side": 1,
      "message": "- this error message is printed if SMC_SC_SCHED_SHARE_UNREGISTER. You have another error message if trusty_reclaim_memory. If you are referring to leaking resources on the Linux side, you don\u0027t need to leak anything here if trusty_reclaim_memory succeeds.\n- the point of these error checks is not to detect problems in Linux, it is to detect problems elsewhere and prevent them from turning into a problem here. For these calls to work correctly the hypervisor(s), el3 and trusty all need to work as expected.\n- returning an error from the driver\u0027s remove function does not trigger a reboot, it is likely to be silently ignored\n\n(PS#12 removes this extra error message though)",
